{"card":{"card_id":"ma-c-04a4d455c185ca821fa0","statement":"Let $\\Delta = - \\Delta$, let $P \\subset \\Delta$ be a strongly parabolic subset of $\\Delta$,\nand let $\\gp$, $\\gl$ and $\\gn$ be as above. The following hold.\n\n- [(i)] $\\gn$ is an ideal of $\\gp$.\n\n- [(ii)] Every irreducible weight $\\gl$--module $N$ is an irreducible weight $\\gp$--module with the trivial action of $\\gn$. Conversely,\nif $N$ is an irreducible weight $\\gp$--module, then $\\gn$ acts trivially on $N$ and $N$ is an irreducible weight $\\gl$--module.\n\n- [(iii)] If $N$ is an irreducible weight $\\gp$--module, then the module $M_\\gp(N) = U(\\gg) \\otimes_{U(\\gp)}  N$ admits a unique\nmaximal proper submodule and, consequently, a unique irreducible quotient $V_\\gp(N)$.","source_id":"arXiv:0904.0041","cluster":"representation_theory","statement_sha256":"7e3bf463769921ea4d0614e67536c0377d4a2517a8350e3439dfa437d84474a8","kind":"proposition","label":"Proposition 3","ref_key":"prop3","name":"","order":8,"deps":[],"cite_keys":[],"provenance":{"source_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/0904.0041","harvest_mode":"arxiv_eprint","payload_sha256":"a14448ebca79573d37a3bacc4abdcb445d514c88d4c650e891ad880c4e25d977","line":451,"origin":"latex_env","retrieved_at":"2026-09-29T14:02:31+08:00"},"wash":{"version":"cardwash.v2","stages":["segment","purify","classify","dedupe","emit"],"numbering":"document_order_with_label_heuristic","detail":{"stripped_proof":false,"chars":674,"math_hints":69}}},"paper":{"source_id":"arXiv:0904.0041","title":"Parabolic sets of roots","abstract":"We compare two combinatorial definitions of parabolic sets of roots. We show that these definitions are equivalent for simple finite dimensional Lie algebras, affine Lie algebras, and toroidal Lie algebras. In contrast, these definitions are not always equivalent for simple finite dimensional Lie superalgebras.","authors":["Ivan Dimitrov","Vyacheslav Futorny","Dimitar Grantcharov"],"year":"2009","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/0904.004